    "The new tests require committed review events and positive document history work, so equal no-op results cannot satisfy their history laws. No current native/protocol behavior, saved format, API/default, core history limit or package version changes.",
    "Native source/runtime bytes and prior native suites remain unchanged and carried explicitly. Fresh exact-source native fixture production, public types, storage contracts, source/installed probes and all 1,525 script tests execute; three existing opt-in skips are not platform qualification.",
    "The explicit --author-conformance flag enforces package-byte identity only for this test-only qualification. The normal portable installed check remains valid for later intentional production changes.",
    "Native ancestor/local-origin/current composition, full provider/client-outbox closure, independent comment-generation sessions, historical-copy disposition and authenticated deployment fencing/activation remain required. No browser/IME/VoiceOver, resource, license, full functional profile or V1 readiness is inferred. Nothing is pushed, published, tagged or deployed."
